Time Complexity:-
Time Complexity describes how much time an algorithm takes to run as the input size increases.
It is represented using Big O notation.


Space Complexity:-
Space Complexity describes how much extra memory an algorithm uses while running.
It includes:
  Variables
  Data structures
  Extra storage

Eg:-

  for i in range(0,6,1):  ---->m+1
      print("Hi")
  for i in range(0,11,1):  ----->n+1
      print("Hi")

  Time complexity = O(n+m) = O(5+10) =O(11) = O(n) 
 Space Complexity=O(1)


